-- title:
--   Realisation of Tₚ in the sub-family corner ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional $k$-representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ factoring through a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline k$) and such that the associated adic representation is ordinary at $p$: over each valuation subring lying over $p$ there is a free rank-one submodule spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, with inertia acting trivially modulo it. Assumed further: a finite set $S$ of primes with $p\in S$; a level $N$ with $p\nmid N$ all of whose prime factors lie in $S$; a subset $Smin\subseteq S$ containing $p$ which, away from $p$, consists exactly of the primes where $\bar\rho$ is ramified, whose members other than $p$ divide $N$, while primes $q\neq p$ outside $Smin$ dividing $N$ satisfy $q^2\mid N$, no $q\neq p$ has $q^3\mid N$, and inertia at each $q\in Smin$, $q\neq p$, has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; an auxiliary prime $r\geq 5$ with $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$ and $\operatorname{tr}\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius element at every valuation subring over $r$; weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by their lattice of forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients. Given a ring homomorphism $\theta_0$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ realising $\bar\rho$, in the sense that for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ is $X^2-\theta_0(T_\ell)X+\ell$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi T_0$ from the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to $\mathcal O$, the subgroup $H_0\leq(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ characterised as the kernel of reduction to $\mathbb Z/r$, a family of scalars $cU$ and a map $\bar\theta$ on the sub-family of generators of level $Nr$ (those $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and diamond operators whose $U$-generators have $q\mid N$) whose operators on $H^1$ commute pairwise, with $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta_0(T_\ell)$, $\bar\theta(U_q)$ the residue of $cU(U_q)$, $\bar\theta(\langle d\rangle)=1$, and $cU(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ whenever $q\mid N$, $q\neq p$, $q^2\mid N$; finally an idempotent splitting $Sp$ of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O))$ generated by these operators, an index $i$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the $i$-th corner ring to $k$ sending the image of each sub-family operator to its $\bar\theta$-value, and the hypothesis that every element of $\Gamma_0(Nr)$ acts as the identity through `diamondRaw` on the corner submodule $e_i\cdot H^1$. Then there exists an element $t_p$ of the corner ring such that multiplication by $t_p$ on the corner submodule agrees with the Hecke operator `heckeT (N * r) H₀ p 𝒪`, and such that for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$, every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $p$ for it, and every $k$-endomorphism $E$ of the inertia coinvariants $\bar\rho.V/\sum_{\tau}\mathrm{range}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ (the sum over inertia at that place) induced by $\bar\rho(\sigma)$, one has $\pi_k(t_p)=\operatorname{tr} E$.
--
--   This is the step supplying the element of the corner Hecke ring at level $Nr$ that realises $T_p$ on the chosen corner, together with the identification of its residue as the trace of Frobenius on the inertia coinvariants of $\bar\rho$ at $p$. It is used by the companion statement which, invoking ordinarity at $p$, asserts in addition that this element is a unit.
